<speak>Mostly through my daughter, actually. She'll send something about a gallery programme or a neighbourhood event and say we should try it. I used to reply that we'd see how the weekend went, which usually meant we didn't go. Now I'm trying to put it in the calendar like any other appointment. Not every weekend, but occasionally. We went to a small exhibition recently, then had dinner nearby. I didn't know much about the subject beforehand, but that turned out not to matter. We enjoyed talking about what we saw.</speak>